@startuml network-flow
title DONUT — Remote operation network routing (resolve -> reconnect -> update -> settle)
' Code-grounded trace. Method names map 1:1 to source so each step is navigable.
' Legend:  green note = bug fixed/hardened   |   tan note = concurrency/modal caveat

skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam noteFontSize 11
' ParticipantPadding/BoxPadding skinparams were dropped: deprecated in PlantUML
' 1.2026.x, which stamps a warning banner onto the rendered SVG.

actor Operator as OP

box "UI thread (WPF dispatcher + ~200ms pump)" #151221
  participant "HomePresenter\n(+ AsyncJobPresenter.PumpJobs)" as P
  participant "HostResolver\n(in-memory cache + latch)" as R
end box

box "Runspace pool (background threads)" #101B14
  participant "AsyncJob\n(PowerShell.BeginInvoke)" as J
  participant "ExecutionService\n(RemoteWorker.ps1)" as W
  participant "NetworkProbe\n(DNS / RPC-135 / SMB-445)" as N
end box

box "Fast resolve lane (direct child pwsh)" #1B1414
  participant "ResolveProcessJob\n(Process.Start -> ResolveWorker.ps1)" as F
end box

box "Target environment" #1E1610
  participant "Domain Controller\n(AD + DNS)" as DC
  participant "Target host\n(admin share + dcu-cli)" as H
end box

== Phase 0 — Warm (startup, once) ==
P -> J : Resolve{Warm}  +  Resolve{WarmRunspace}
J -> W : StartWorker -> RunResolvePhase
W -> N : GetActiveDomainController()
N -> DC : Get-ADDomainController + IsOnline
W -> W : WarmRuntimeAssemblies()\n(exercise DNS/CIM/TCP/LDAP against localhost so no live\njob pays a first-use cost; the barrier parks + reaps an\noverrunning warm, so a wedge here can't hold up the app)
J --> P : CompleteResolve -> Resolver.SetActiveDc(dc)
note over P,R #13291D
  Warm loads the heavy assemblies + the worker class graph into EVERY
  pool runspace so no job ever cold-loads under the process-wide CLR
  loader lock (which stalls the WPF dispatcher = UI freeze).
  [FIXED] the pool is now PINNED (min = max): its idle cleanup
  (15 min) only reaps runspaces above min, so previously all but one
  warmed runspace died after 15 idle minutes - and the next
  CONCURRENT job (e.g. storage scan mid DCU-scan) landed on a fresh
  cold runspace and froze the UI. Pinned, the warm holds for life.
end note

== Phase 1 — Resolve a host (start-early, on select; the FAST LANE) ==
OP -> P : select row  (SelectHost)
P -> R : NeedsResolve(host)? (DC known, not in-flight, uncached OR stale)
alt needs resolve
  P -> R : MarkInFlight(host)
  P -> F : slim ResolveWorker child (DIRECT spawn - no pool slot)
  note right of F #13291D
    Fast lane: capped at 4 concurrent children (FIFO overflow queue);
    no worker module graph, so ~1-2s instead of ~2.5-5s + pool wait.
    A ProcessFault (crash/kill/timeout) retries ONCE on the classic
    RemoteWorker path; 3 consecutive faults latch the lane off.
  end note
  F -> DC : Resolve-DnsName -Server dc  (A record, authoritative)
  F -> H : connect 135  (TCP, bounded 2s, breadcrumb logged pre-connect)
  F --> P : CompleteResolve  (verdict JSON via result file)
  alt job Failed (HadErrors, e.g. DNS/RPC errored)
    P -> R : ClearInFlight(host)
    note right of R #13291D
      [FIXED] a failed resolve now RELEASES the single-flight latch.
      Previously it leaked -> NeedsResolve stuck false forever ->
      host wedged on "Resolving ... - run again in a moment".
    end note
  else job Completed
    P -> R : CacheVerdict(host, ip, online)  (stamps CheckedAt for the 5-min TTL)
    P -> P : RenderReachability + GatherInventoryIfOnline (selected host only)
  end
end

== Phase 2 — Inventory (select / double-click) ==
P -> P : StartInventory(host)
P -> R : IsHostOnline(host) + IsVerdictStale(host)
alt Offline
  P -> P : skip ("host is offline")
else Unknown OR stale 'Online'
  P -> P : PrefetchIp(host)  (re-verify off-thread; re-gather when the fresh verdict lands)
  note right of P #13291D
    [FIXED] gather no longer trusts an aged-out 'Online' verdict
    (IsHostOnline ignored the TTL) -> avoids opening the freeze-prone
    connect against a host that has since gone offline.
  end note
else fresh Online
  P -> J : Inventory
  J -> W : RunInventoryPhase
  W -> N : IsRpcAvailable(ip) (2s gate)
  W -> H : New-CimSession (DCOM, -OperationTimeoutSec 15)  -> Win32_* fast path
  note right of W #13291D
    [FIXED] both CIM opens (inventory + the identity name query) are
    bounded by -OperationTimeoutSec 15 - a box that died after the RPC
    gate fails in seconds, not DCOM's multi-minute defaults.
  end note
  W -> H : psexec probe fallback (if CIM empty/blocked)
  note right of W #13291D
    [FIXED] the probe psexec (also used by the WizTree disk scan) now
    has the -n 60 connect timeout and classifies exit codes by cause
    (launch fault / transport drop / real failure) like the dcu-cli path.
  end note
  note right of W #13291D
    [FIXED] every psexec launch uses a per-job-family service name
    (-r DonutDcu / DonutDisk / DonutProbe): concurrent sessions to the
    SAME host used to share one PSEXESVC, and when the first finished
    it deleted the service under the second - which then hung forever.
    A worker WATCHDOG also kills the local psexec client past a per-job
    deadline (scan 30m / apply 120m / probe 10m / disk 20m) -> typed
    RemoteTimeoutException instead of a forever-Running job that blocks
    the single-flight guard.
  end note
  J --> P : CompleteInventory -> memoize reports\ JSON -> card
end

== Phase 3 — Run (scan / apply), "from where left off" ==
OP -> P : Run  (StartProcess, active command)
P -> R : IsHostOnline(host) + IsVerdictStale(host)
alt Offline
  P -> P : skip + toast ("host is offline")
else Unknown OR stale 'Online'
  P -> R : PendingRuns[host] = queued ; PrefetchIp (re-verify off-thread)
  R --> P : CompleteResolve (fresh verdict) -> auto-StartProcess / skip-with-toast / drop-with-reason
  note right of P #13291D
    [FIXED] a missing OR aged-out 'Online' verdict is re-verified first
    and the run is QUEUED - it starts automatically once the fresh
    verdict lands. Offline -> skipped with a toast; failed resolve ->
    dropped with a reason. Never queued silently, no second Run click.
  end note
else fresh Online
  alt scan cached < 24h (RecentScanIsFresh)  — resume, don't rescan
    P -> P : reuse scan -> ProceedWithApply (skips Phase-1 rescan)
  else fresh scan needed
    P -> J : UpdateScan
    P -> J : Resolve{Name}  (StartVerifyName — parallel identity check, applyUpdates mode only)
    J -> W : RunScanPhase -> InvokePsExec  (ResolvedIpFor: seeded IP; un-seeded fallback now logs a slow-path warning)
    W -> N : InvokePsExec SMB gate -> IsSmbAvailable(ip) (445, 2s) — the ONLY pre-launch touch
    W -> H : psexec -s -h  pwsh -EncodedCommand (BuildRemoteDcuScript: discover dcu-cli on target, clear + /scan)
    W -> H : live-tail scan.log while psexec runs (each tick SMB-gated 2s) -> Information stream\n(scan steps "N/5" + percents -> card bar; every line -> detail terminal)
    W -> H : CopyRemoteArtifacts (scan.log + newest *.xml report;\nSMB-gated with a brief retry - warns + skips instead of hanging)
    J --> P : Complete(UpdateScan)
  end
end

== Phase 4 — Apply pipeline (ProceedWithApply) ==
P -> R : IdentityVerdict(host)  (from the parallel Name check)
alt Mismatch  (the IP now answers as a different machine)
  P -> P : ABORT apply + InvalidateResolved (drop IP, re-resolve)
else Match OR Unknown
  note right of P #13291D
    [HARDENED] the dialog now STATES the verdict ("identity verified
    as X" / "not verified yet - proceed with care"), and it is
    RE-CHECKED after the dialog closes (the pump keeps draining the
    parallel name-check while it's open) - a late Mismatch aborts
    before the destructive step. 'Unknown' proceeds by design.
  end note
  P -> P : parse report -> driver match -> ShowConfirmation (MODAL, + identity line)
  note over P #2A2211
    Modal opens inside the pump. IsModalOpen() then DEFERS other jobs'
    completions to a later non-modal tick (avoids stacked dialogs).
  end note
  OP -> P : confirm
  P -> R : re-check IdentityVerdict  (late Mismatch -> ABORT + re-resolve)
  P -> J : UpdateApply
  J -> W : RunApplyPhase -> InvokePsExec
  W -> N : InvokePsExec SMB gate -> IsSmbAvailable(ip) (445, 2s) — the ONLY pre-launch touch
  W -> H : psexec: pwsh -EncodedCommand (BuildRemoteDcuScript: kill DCU, discover dcu-cli, clear apply.log, /applyUpdates)
  W -> H : live-tail apply.log while psexec runs (each tick SMB-gated 2s) -> Information stream\n(percent lines drive the determinate bar; every line -> detail terminal)
  note right of W #13291D
    [FIXED] NO controller-side UNC before launch. dcu-cli discovery and the
    pre-run log clear both run ON the target (BuildRemoteDcuScript), so an
    open-but-wedged C$ share (e.g. a host mid-reboot after a BIOS flash) can
    no longer stall the worker before psexec is even sent. The remote clear
    runs after killing any live DCU, so a recovered code is always this run's.
    A missing dcu-cli returns the $DcuNotFoundExit sentinel -> DcuNotInstalled.
  end note
end

== Phase 5 — Reconnect / recover (psexec exit code) ==
H --> W : psexec exit code
alt exit < 0  (NTSTATUS, e.g. 0xC0000142)
  W -> J : throw RemoteProcessStartException  (remote pwsh never ran)
else transport code  (233 / 64 / 59 UNEXP_NET_ERR / 1232 HOST_UNREACHABLE / ...)
  note right of W #13291D
    [FIXED] the drop can be at EITHER end: the target's NIC reset (a network-driver
    install), or the operator's OWN laptop losing Wi-Fi (59/1232/...). dcu-cli keeps
    running on the target regardless, so the run does not fail - it reconnects + resumes.
  end note
  W -> W : RecoverByResumeTail (bounded AppConfig.GetRecoveryWindowMinutes ~30m, backoff 5->60s)
  loop until code found OR window elapsed
    W -> W : IsLocalOnline? no -> emit "[reconnect] this machine is offline…" (card: Reconnecting)
    W -> H : IsSmbAvailable? no -> emit "[reconnect] reconnecting to <target>…"
    W -> H : reachable -> TailAndScanLog: RESUME tail from last seenChars\n(stream missed lines) + DcuLog.ParseReturnCode
  end
  alt N in {0,1,5}   -> reconnected + confirmed (1/5 = reboot)
    W --> J : return N
  else N is a real DCU error
    W -> J : throw RemoteExecutionException(N, decoded)
  else window elapsed, no code (mid-install / laptop died)
    W -> J : throw RemoteConnectionLostException  (amber "Unconfirmed"; re-scan)
  end
else normal exit N
  alt N in {0,1,5}
    note right of W #13291D
      [FIXED] classification: ONLY {0,1,5} are success/reboot.
      2 (unknown err), 3 (not Dell), 4 (not admin), 6/7/8, 100+, 500+
      are ERRORS — they were previously swallowed as success.
    end note
    W --> J : return N   (RunApplyPhase sets RebootRequired = NeedsReboot(N))
  else error
    W -> J : throw RemoteExecutionException(N, DcuLog.DescribeReturnCode(N))
  end
end

== Phase 6 — Settle / persist / notify ==
J --> P : OnJobCompleted(job)
alt UpdateApply Completed
  P -> P : CheckForManualReboot(job) -> reads result.RebootRequired -> ManualRebootQueue
  note right of P #13291D
    [FIXED] reboot detection previously watched a flag file nothing
    writes + regex-matched a hashtable -> a reboot-required apply
    always showed green "Completed" and never toasted.
  end note
end
alt job Failed
  P -> P : ReflectFailure — offline-class reasons (Offline /\nUnresolvable / ConnectionLost / TimedOut) flip the host's\nverdict + repaint the row BEFORE the retry
  P -> R : InvalidateResolved (drop IP + PrefetchIp) — the re-probe\nconfirms the offline or self-corrects a transient
  P -> P : ShowError toast
end
P -> P : SettleHost -> Store.Upsert(status, updateCount) [recents.json]
note over P #1F1F26
  Card state: Completed(green) / RebootRequired(yellow) /
  ConnectionLost(amber "Unconfirmed") / Offline(grey) / Failed(red).
  The dot renders through ONE precedence (attention > offline >
  online > idle, same mapper as the sort), verdicts older than the
  resolve TTL re-probe on the 30s idle tick, and a failed re-resolve
  paints Unknown - reachability never silently rots.
end note
P -> P : AfterPump -> FlushSave (coalesced 1 write/batch)
note right of P #13291D
  [FIXED] reboot-required is announced ONCE, per host, at apply
  completion (toast + yellow card); SettleHost consumes the queue
  entry after persisting it. The redundant batch notice - which
  double-toasted and only fired when the whole batch drained - is gone.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#13291D> green | bug fixed / hardened (all audit hotspots resolved) |
  |<#2A2211> tan   | concurrency / modal note |
endlegend
@enduml
